ode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:14:03-07:00","id":951906,"title":"","content":"Killing people is so wasteful. Hunters are often people with limited capabilities and limited resources, so they can use any help that they can get. Dominate people to leave hints that will lead the hunters to your enemies or to innocent people who annoy you. Arrange for the hunter to find 'evidence' that a local politician is an Infernalist who is sacrificing babies to Satan and, after the hunter kills him, the entire weight of the justice system will come down on the hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:18:01-07:00","id":951913,"title":"","content":"Is their a way a garou can do that? since most of their mind control magics focus on inflaming or dampening emotions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:56:38-07:00","id":951944,"title":"","content":"No, but that is where Kinfolk come into play, especially against a public figure like a politician. Have your Kinfolk them dig up the grave of a recently dead baby, 6:1,000 live births result in death in the USA, and have them put it into cold storage. Have them drop clues in the places where the hunters often frequent. Have them mail a letter without a return address with a lock of hair and a name of the recently dead baby. Have them use burner cell phones to call up the hunters with anonymous tips. Have them leave...parts in the trash of the politician for the hunters to find in the middle of the night. Eventually, the hunter will bite and will attack the politician, one way or another, and will potentially get rid of an inconvenient politician for you and, potentially, give the local police a reason to get rid of the hunter for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:29:04-07:00","id":952084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=951944#post951944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but that is where Kinfolk come into play, especially against a public figure like a politician. Have your Kinfolk them dig up the grave of a recently dead baby, 6:1,000 live births result in death in the USA, and have them put it into cold storage. Have them drop clues in the places where the hunters often frequent. Have them mail a letter without a return address with a lock of hair and a name of the recently dead baby. Have them use burner cell phones to call up the hunters with anonymous tips. Have them leave...parts in the trash of the politician for the hunters to find in the middle of the night. Eventually, the hunter will bite and will attack the politician, one way or another, and will potentially get rid of an inconvenient politician for you and, potentially, give the local police a reason to get rid of the hunter for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because most hunters won't be able to figure out they are getting played by a third party?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T16:05:22-07:00","id":952112,"title":"","content":"Nope. What would you do if you found parts of babies in the garbage of a local politician? Would you honestly think that it was a conspiracy? Or would you think that you had discovered the evidence that a closet serial killer was getting careless?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T16:19:54-07:00","id":952119,"title":"","content":"After some random person sent them information to look for said baby parts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  auto correct 08-16-2016, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:16:39-07:00","id":952148,"title":"","content":"Funny, on my game our troupe of werewolves killed a human and his wife. leaving only the couple's youngest kid alive to witness everything, while we argued what to do with the kid. all i said was &quot;We killed them because they were on our way, they defended themselves.. We are the monsters, we deserve to die.&quot; i wanted to let that kid live so he could grow up and have his chance to avenge his family. We ruined his life...<br /> then, the Theurge Children of Gaia of the party, got closer to the little kid and snapped his neck, she shrugged off and said &quot;Done, problem solved.&quot;<br /> <br /> That was a really dark moment of our game...when it comes to hunters, i always believed they have the moral upper ground","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:14:39-07:00","id":952185,"title":"","content":"That would be a violation of multiple forms of Renown. Heck, as an ST, I would have reduced that particular Children of Gaia by three permanent Glory and Honor and everyone else in the pack one permanent Glory and Honor for associating with that particular Children of Gaia. In fact, that level of gratuitous murder would warrant the performance of The Hunt against the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 08-16-2016, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:54:20-07:00","id":952197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=952185#post952185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be a violation of multiple forms of Renown. Heck, as an ST, I would have reduced that particular Children of Gaia by three permanent Glory and Honor and everyone else in the pack one permanent Glory and Honor for associating with that particular Children of Gaia. In fact, that level of gratuitous murder would warrant the performance of The Hunt against the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>The player was the youngest of our troupe and also the most inmature (seing werewolf almost as a Hellsing esque rpg). Her character was punished with carrying the Stone of Shame (dunno if its canon or was made by the ST), as well ended up being blinded with Silver.<br /> <br /> the rest of the party thought that what she did was horryfing. while she thought it was &quot;ok, i mean. humans are savaging mother gaia. keeping them down is what we do.&quot; my nuwisha intervineed by slapping her in the face saying &quot;No, what we do is fight the wyrm. That human wasnt involved in the war in any ways. besides, wheres the heart of gaia when needed anwyays?&quot; she went like &quot;how dare you to put gaia in this. if she loved this humans so much, she would have save them from being in our path.&quot; the leader went like &quot;healer, heal thyself, huh?&quot; she never understood what was wrong with killing innocent humans, for her. they were just in the middle ground of our arguments but they didnt mattered....im surprised that her char never turned into a black spiral","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T19:05:51-07:00","id":952206,"title":"","content":"Ouch, though it is a light sentence for her crimes. I am surprised a Nuwisha would have stayed in the group after that, the actions of that character would have proven every Garou stereotype to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T09:40:20-07:00","id":952570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=952206#post952206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ouch, though it is a light sentence for her crimes. I am surprised a Nuwisha would have stayed in the group after that, the actions of that character would have proven every Garou stereotype to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>i gave that party the lesson of their life. i pulled the GM to a side and told him<br /> Joe: &quot;i want to bend the rules, i want you to turn me into a black spiral dancer or a fomori.&quot; <br /> Gm :&quot;W-what? b-but youre a nuwisha, i mean, its impossible dude.&quot;<br /> Joe: &quot;youre the fucking GM, nothing is impossible Dude, whenever we go through hives im the only one who takes it as a stroll through the park, making jokes and such. i know i dont have rage or anything that can help me to even out the combat. im the support of the party.&quot;<br /> GM: &quot;Ok?...so..why?&quot;<br /> Joe: &quot;to prove a point.&quot;<br /> Gm: &quot; Continue &quot;<br /> Joe: &quot;Kiragakash (the Child of Gaia) believes that she can still go around as if nothing happend. as if she was completely safe from the darkness of the wyrm after what she did.&quot;<br /> GM: thats why i want to turn her into a fomori with out realizing it<br /> Joe: dont, that will give power to her character. she will see it as a gift and not as a curse. its more painful when the loveable prankster falls into corruption right infront of their eyes, specially if its for a selfish reason<br /> gm: ...you understand your character will die?<br /> joe: yes, but make Her kill my character.<br /> GM: so whats the lesson?<br /> Joe: the wyrm can take you any time, and the price will be heavy.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, i sacrificed a character to teach a lesson in blood.....So remember kiddies, when you mess with hunters. your whole morale will end up fucked up beyond repair","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:49:12-07:00","id":952611,"title":"","content":"the best thing for a garou to do with a Hunter is to try pointing them at some group of skull pigs, formori , Kindred Whatever Maybe give them a bit of helpful info...<br /> <br /> but some Garou have massive egos, they want to stroke.<br /> <br /> will the &quot;Intimidation&quot; system found on W20 279, probaly be enough to cow someone enough for these purposes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T11:01:09-07:00","id":952620,"title":"","content":"I think the best way for any supernatural creature to deal with hunters is to lead them to their enemies. The majority of hunters do not have specific Lore skills, they are just working with Occult, so they do not really know anything beyond the basics (werewolves hate silver, vampires hate sunlight, wraiths are dead people, demons possess people, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T11:03:41-07:00","id":952622,"title":"","content":"Do &quot;Lupine Lore&quot; &quot;Vampire&quot; &quot;Faerie Lore&quot; still exist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T11:27:21-07:00","id":952636,"title":"","content":"If they cause much collaterol damage among the kine, a painful death, and if not a quick death. I'm not really into prolonged torture for different reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T12:03:37-07:00","id":952651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=952622#post952622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do &amp;quot;Lupine Lore&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Vampire&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Faerie Lore&amp;quot; still exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there is also a merit called scholar of others and scholar of enemies. Can't recall what they do off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:14:20-07:00","id":952701,"title":"","content":"They give a -2 difficulty on any non-combat rolls concerning your specialty and a +1 difficulty on any non-combat rolls not concerning your specialty. So I imagine that you could have Scholar of Garou, since they are technically enemies of your Sect, which would allow you a -2 difficulty to socialize, track, understand, etc the Garou, but you would have a +1 difficulty on non-combat rolls dealing with every other supernatural enemy of your Sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T14:16:47-07:00","id":953419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted#post854312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominate... can obviously be used on those close to a hunter.<br /> <br /> Think Conditionings effects are impossible to disguise?</div> </div> </div> </div> They are. Dominate has a tendency to blunt your subject's capacity for rational or creative thought; repeated applications of the discipline against the same person - which is what conditioning <i>is</i> - has a tendency to gradually turn the person into a mindlessly quiescent puppet. So, yes, if anyone's paying even the <i>remotest</i> amount of attention, they'll notice.<br /> <br /> As for the core question...<br /> <br /> It's ultimately a fairly simple matter to cause someone more pain - be it physical, psychological or both - than they can bear, assuming you hold absolute power over them. Assuming there's nowhere they can go for help, and no place they can retreat to that is safe from you, you can assault their weak points without particular issue.<br /> <br /> It's ultimately quite trivial for any of the supernaturals to casually destroy a mortal's life, after all, and the number of ways in which can be done are virtually infinite. Really, it's not so much a question of &quot;how do we do this&quot; as &quot;how <i>can't</i> we do this&quot;.<br /> <br /> Rather than killing a mortal's loved ones, a Kindred could instead blood bond them - force the hunter to watch their beloved child, or sister, or lover, fall desperately and hopelessly in love with an undead horror that cares nothing for them, or simply apply Dominate like the mental sledgehammer that it so frequently is to reduce the consistency of said loved one's soul to paste.<br /> <br /> Simply ask yourself what you would give <i>anything</i> to avoid happening to you, and there you pretty much have your answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=952148#post952148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny, on my game our troupe of werewolves killed a human and his wife. leaving only the couple's youngest kid alive to witness everything, while we argued what to do with the kid. all i said was &quot;We killed them because they were on our way, they defended themselves.. We are the monsters, we deserve to die.&quot; i wanted to let that kid live so he could grow up and have his chance to avenge his family. We ruined his life...<br /> then, the Theurge Children of Gaia of the party, got closer to the little kid and snapped his neck, she shrugged off and said &quot;Done, problem solved.&quot;<br /> <br /> That was a really dark moment of our game...when it comes to hunters, i always believed they have the moral upper ground</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd be interested to know what the circumstances were that made it necessary for a full pack of werewolves to engage a single mortal couple in full view of their child.<br /> <br /> I do somewhat think that saying &quot;hunters have the moral high ground&quot; is a bit simplistic, though; &quot;hunter&quot; is ultimately an incredibly broad umbrella that encompasses everything from the proverbial lost orphan child seeking the slayer of his parents to the crazed lunatics that will kill all non-humans simply for the crime of being non-humans.<br /> <br /> Does the shotgun-toting religious fanatic pumping shells into the beds of defenceless kinfolk children hold the moral high ground over the staunch Child of Gaia fighting desperately every night to save the world from falling into darkness? What about a man who sees all vampires as monsters plunging a hatchet into a Tremere doctor and biothaumaturge who uses the power of his blood sorcery to save terminal patients who otherwise could never be saved, sparing their families - potentially dozens of people - needless agony? Who holds the high ground there? Murderer or victim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T15:05:11-07:00","id":953442,"title":"","content":"Hunters can be more evil than the 'monsters' they go after. That being said, it is almost always better to send a hunter after your enemy than to kill them. If you are a vampire, however, ghouling all of their family and then leaving them at 1 blood pool is fun because they will have 1 die to resist frenzy. The hunter will have to watch as their entire family goes crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T15:43:52-07:00","id":953455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seviphas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=953419#post953419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They are. Dominate has a tendency to blunt your subject's capacity for rational or creative thought; repeated applications of the discipline against the same person - which is what conditioning <i>is</i> - has a tendency to gradually turn the person into a mindlessly quiescent puppet. So, yes, if anyone's paying even the <i>remotest</i> amount of attention, they'll notice.<br /> <br /> As for the core question...<br /> <br /> It's ultimately a fairly simple matter to cause someone more pain - be it physical, psychological or both - than they can bear, assuming you hold absolute power over them. Assuming there's nowhere they can go for help, and no place they can retreat to that is safe from you, you can assault their weak points without particular issue.<br /> <br /> It's ultimately quite trivial for any of the supernaturals to casually destroy a mortal's life, after all, and the number of ways in which can be done are virtually infinite. Really, it's not so much a question of &quot;how do we do this&quot; as &quot;how <i>can't</i> we do this&quot;.<br /> <br /> Rather than killing a mortal's loved ones, a Kindred could instead blood bond them - force the hunter to watch their beloved child, or sister, or lover, fall desperately and hopelessly in love with an undead horror that cares nothing for them, or simply apply Dominate like the mental sledgehammer that it so frequently is to reduce the consistency of said loved one's soul to paste.<br /> <br /> Simply ask yourself what you would give <i>anything</i> to avoid happening to you, and there you pretty much have your answer.<br /> <br /> I'd be interested to know what the circumstances were that made it necessary for a full pack of werewolves to engage a single mortal couple in full view of their child.<br /> <br /> I do somewhat think that saying &quot;hunters have the moral high ground&quot; is a bit simplistic, though; &quot;hunter&quot; is ultimately an incredibly broad umbrella that encompasses everything from the proverbial lost orphan child seeking the slayer of his parents to the crazed lunatics that will kill all non-humans simply for the crime of being non-humans.<br /> <br /> Does the shotgun-toting religious fanatic pumping shells into the beds of defenceless kinfolk children hold the moral high ground over the staunch Child of Gaia fighting desperately every night to save the world from falling into darkness? What about a man who sees all vampires as monsters plunging a hatchet into a Tremere doctor and biothaumaturge who uses the power of his blood sorcery to save terminal patients who otherwise could never be saved, sparing their families - potentially dozens of people - needless agony? Who holds the high ground there? Murderer or victim?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A fantasy of mine for a bit? <br /> <br /> has been a Pentex Formori who grew up in a slum, his parents were slaughtered in front of him by a Silver Fang, Shadow Lord, or Fianna Pack<br /> <br /> and he makes a big deal about &quot;Earning&quot; his position ranting regularly about how wrong classism is etc<br /> <br /> because I felt it could be eye opening as usualy cases of Rich against poor, put the rich in the bad guy role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T16:09:23-07:00","id":953469,"title":"","content":"And that justifies the cannibalistic, rapine, murderous behavior of the Pentex fomori how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:21:16-07:00","id":953544,"title":"","content":"in no shape or form<br /> <br /> the goal is to make him a tragic figure, not neccessarily &quot;In the right&quot; <br /> <br /> If you've ever watched the Anime &quot;Detective conan&quot; (In the states it was released uner the name &quot;Case Closed&quot; its a mysterry anime, and rather goofy when not dealing with the actualy mysterry cases... but in the murder cases, it gets fairly serious, the protaganist Pities the murderers almost as much as their victims, but never hesitates to accuse them.<br /> <br /> to help preserve the peace and stability of Japan.<br /> <br /> And some of the murderers are tear jerkingly sympathetic.<br /> <br /> Murder on the Orient Express... ok so in my mind what they did WAS justified morally if not legally, they teamed up and murdered a guy who murdered their friends baby... still its the only non anime reference I can think of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:25:58-07:00","id":953621,"title":"","content":"Yes, but they are rarely rapists or cannibals. Pentex Fomori are serial killers, I think you would have to go with an Independent Fomori to get a sympathetic murderer. I have had great success with Independent Fomori in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:36:30-07:00","id":953627,"title":"","content":"oh you've watched Detective conan? <br /> <br /> Youve got a point, but theirs that and also to create a moment where a clearer head might see that the pig headedness of the Garou involved helped to give the wyrm a soldier.<br /> <br /> does that make sense.<br /> <br /> Thats the point as much as any sympathy for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T06:48:13-07:00","id":953804,"title":"","content":"Strangely enough, I never had many problems with my players killing civilians. It was always considered to be a potential breach of the Veil that would hurt local canine populations to leave evidence of an unnecessary kill, so my players made sure to kill after capture. People would be blackbagged if they were found to work for the Wyrm, killed with a plant poison, and then dropped off in a suburban neighborhood in the middle of the night. Hunters who got too close to kinfolk were treated much in the same way, though there were often efforts to redirect their attention to the enemies of the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T08:48:10-07:00","id":953871,"title":"","content":"Also Aya Tari, ever read freak legion? a lot of its been retconned but it does a goodjob of painting Formori as sympathetic, even pentex Formori.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T13:44:18-07:00","id":954007,"title":"","content":"I have it. That was before they introduced Autonomy though, so there was no way to represent the spectrum of corruption, which is what Pentex exploits. An Autonomy 8-9 Fomori is still human enough to care about things, but Pentex encourages them to drop their Autonomy so that the bane eventually gets control over the Fomori (Banes tend to have an average Willpower of 6, so they need the Autonomy of the Fomori to average around 5 to allow the Bane to control things). A Fomori with an Autonomy of 5 is a weapon, pure and simple, which is released to cause terror and pain upon the local population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T14:24:39-07:00","id":954040,"title":"","content":"I dont remember everything, but I do remember that the lower autonamy gets the lower your willpower max is...<br /> <br /> my problem with possessed was Kami are so screwed over, in that without an autonamy trait, they couldnt buy new powers without buying taints...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T15:59:18-07:00","id":954083,"title":"","content":"Yeah, which was really screwy because the Kami examples in Possessed have too many powers for their taints. I would actually allow Kami to purchase powers during character creation for 1 freebie point per power point or after character creation for 2 experience points per power point. I think that would allow Kami to be more playable and would reflect the examples in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T00:31:21-07:00","id":956836,"title":"","content":"Are we talking hunters, or Hunters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T06:29:09-07:00","id":956910,"title":"","content":"either, though bonus points for Hunters, as its so hard to put them in their place cant just dominate them into kneeling, so ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T06:57:15-07:00","id":956924,"title":"","content":"I think that you have to turn the system against Hunters. When Hunters start having to run from the authorities, when they start having to kill innocent humans to stay free, that is when you start breaking them. If they end up in prison, so much the better, as you have so many people that you can bribe to make the Hunter suffer.<br /> <br /> It is easy enough for vampires to kill a human child, leave the corpse in the trunk of the car of a Hunter, and then leave a tip on the police hotline. What is the Hunter going to say? That the vampires did it? If they are lucky, the judge will put them in a prison of the criminally insane for the rest of their life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T16:37:21-07:00","id":957264,"title":"","content":"Anything that a High humanity Vamp can do just out of curiousity?<br /> <br /> Wont WANT to put anyone &quot;In their place&quot; but might want to protect themselves from Hunters<br /> <br /> and to show hunters that their just putting themselves in unneccessary danger and might wind up putting their family in danger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 08-24-2016, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T18:34:00-07:00","id":957309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=957264#post957264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything that a High humanity Vamp can do just out of curiousity?<br /> <br /> Wont WANT to put anyone &quot;In their place&quot; but might want to protect themselves from Hunters<br /> <br /> and to show hunters that their just putting themselves in unneccessary danger and might wind up putting their family in danger.</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends on how liberally your ST interprets the hierarchy of sins, honestly.<br /> <br /> If, by &quot;high humanity&quot;, you mean 8-10, then... no, not really, there's not actually very much you can do to defend yourself. At humanity 8 you're actually prohibited from the use of force in self-defence - &quot;injury to another, accidental or otherwise&quot; - meaning that your options at that point are flight or surrender. Certainly, you probably do have the faculties simply to escape from a hunter who is looking to harm you - Potence lets you put obstacles between you and anybody chasing you, Celerity lets you outrun them, Presence or Dominate can compel your would-be slayer not to harm you...<br /> <br /> If your ST allows the use of defensive force at high humanity, then you can do a lot - and if you're 7 or lower you can in any event do a great deal to discourage somebody from hunting you. You can do anything but outright kill them, after all - breaking limbs, causing severe but non-fatal injuries, these are all fair game by RAW.<br /> <br /> Now, me, if I had a high humanity vampire that was being hunted, and said vampire repeatedly warned the hunter to stay away, gave 'em ample chances to back off, and then when there was no choice remaining but to kill them or be themselves slain, I'd give that vampire fairly hefty bonuses to any degeneration roll that followed if they indeed resorted to lethal force in the end. They did everything they could, after all, and in my games that counts for something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T19:55:19-07:00","id":957348,"title":"","content":"Well, there are ways. Humanity deals with your direct actions or the actions done by people that you control, not the actions done by people who are not under your control. If you are a high Humanity vampire, create a false trail (such as animal corpses that are drained of blood) to a lower Humanity vampire that will not be as kind. You could also leave hints for the local gang members that the Hunter is hiding a major stash of drugs, money, or weapons, which would convince them to rob the Hunter's house, which would distract the Hunter and may deprive the Hunter of essential resources.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if the Hunter has illegal weapons, you could alert the local authorities that there is a terrorist (which the Hunter technically is) preparing on a major assault against one of the local government offices. The shifty behavior of the Hunter will probably make the police suspicious, so they will get a warrant, and the Hunter is then held on weapons violations (which is rather major, even in the USA, if the Hunter does not have the appropriate permits and receipts for the weapons). If you want to really screw over the Hunter, buy stolen weapons from the local criminal syndicate, break into his house, plant the weapons, and then tip off the police (if the weapons happened to be one linked to a cop killing, so much the better).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T23:22:31-07:00","id":957429,"title":"","content":"Only a technical reading of humanity views luring someone to a particularly gruesome death, or arranging for them to be murdered, as not a sin of the path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:21:58-07:00","id":957606,"title":"","content":"How are you responsible for the actions of either the Hunter or the Vampire? How are you responsible for the actions of the gangs or the police? You are only responsible for your actions or the actions of the entities under your control. Would you be at fault if you reported the suspicious activity of the Hunter to the cops and, during the confrontation, the Hunter killed a cop or was killed by a cop?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:37:12-07:00","id":957614,"title":"","content":"If you deliberately set someone up to be killed, you do bear moral responsibility for that death. If I lure a child with candy into the den of a rabid wolf, is my sin lesser for not killing them with my own hands?<br /> <br /> I would argue the opposite. My sin is not lessened but rather it is made greater for subjecting them to not only a death, but a particularly terrifying, cruel one. The same applies for a vampire. Taking an action that you know will take their life, or will predictably result in the taking of their life by another, is no different than snapping their neck with your own hands save that you aren't the last person to see them alive. Arguably, it is an even more grotesque sin because you involve a third party and cause them moral injury - at best an injury to another, at worst, a second planned violation. If it causes them to die in significantly more pain than you yourself would inflict, it is an even greater sin - albeit one it may be easier to live with.<br /> <br /> It is one thing to report a hunter to the police and let come what may. It is another to report them after planting a gun used to kill another cop, knowing the likely consequences and deliberately seeking them out. I remind you that Humanity 3 sins are not merely described as murder, but the planned violation of another. Arranging their painful death is planned, premeditated, and a violation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:16:08-07:00","id":957654,"title":"","content":"I lean towards the Calling the police, maybe greese the wheels and help the police find well hidden things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:37:46-07:00","id":957700,"title":"","content":"So I am guilty of the sins of people I do not control? Am I guilty of murder if I sell someone the guns they use to kill their wife? Am I guilty of murder if I sell someone the beer that sends them into alcohol poisoning? Am I guilty of murder if I break up with someone and that causes them to commit suicide? When are the people who make the murderous or suicidal decisions guilty of their actions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 08-25-2016, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T10:55:32-07:00","id":957708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=957700#post957700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am guilty of the sins of people I do not control?</div> </div> </div> </div> Control is not a binary switch; you wield differing degrees of influence over all the people you know, and to a certain extent if you use that influence to push those people towards certain actions, <i>yes</i><i>, </i>you bear some of the guilt for their sins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=957700#post957700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I guilty of murder if I sell someone the guns they use to kill their wife?</div> </div> </div> </div> If you knew, or reasonably believed, that they intended to use the weapons for that purpose? You're pretty guilty in my books, yeah. If you shrug your shoulders and cheerfully help someone along the path to committing evil acts, then you're an accomplice, and you are to blame. I mean, how does that saying go? <i>All that's required for the triumph of evil...</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=957700#post957700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I guilty of murder if I sell someone the beer that sends them into alcohol poisoning?</div> </div> </div> </div> Legally, I really have no idea. Morally? Again, if they were wasted off their face, barely functional at the time, or if you already knew that person as an alcoholic two steps from a sticky end? Yup. You bet your ass you share some of the blame. They may be responsible for that ultimate choice, but that doesn't absolve you as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=957700#post957700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I guilty if I break up with someone and that causes them to commit suicide?</div> </div> </div> </div> Certainly, some of the causal responsibility for their death lies with you, yes. However, this departs from the earlier examples in that terminating a relationship with someone is effectively a cessation of a sequence of positive acts on your behalf; you're not doing something so much as you are <i>ceasing</i> to do something - that is, give an unstable person your affection and support, which I would argue that you have no particular obligation to do.<br /> <br /> The other examples concern positive acts that you deliberately undertook that brought about bad ends - if you help a depressed person to climb onto a rooftop from which they then leap, is it not partially because of you that they died? After all, but for your actions they may have changed their minds upon being unable to complete their ascent and walked down a different path entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:49:37-07:00","id":957782,"title":"","content":"But people have control over their actions and, even if you can reasonably predict their responses, they bear the entire weight of guilt for their actions as long as they are not under your control. A Hunter has a choice to invade the lair of a vampire when the only evidence is a trail of drained animal bodies. A Hunter has the choice to oppose the gang members or to surrender his money or weapons. A Hunter has the choice to attack the police when they arrest him or to trust in the judicial system (planted weapons will likely not lead to the death of the Hunter, though it may lead to his imprisonment).<br /> <br /> If a Hunter chooses to observe the lair of the less humane vampire and interferes when that vampire drags a helpless victim into their lair (or follows them on their hunting rounds and saves an innocent when the less humane vampire attacks them), then several good things may happen. First, the Hunter may save an innocent that you, as the humane vampire, could not save because you might harm the other vampire. Second, the Hunter may kill the inhumane vampire, potentially saving dozens or hundreds of innocent lives in the future, which you could not have done. Third, the Hunter may decide that he found the vampire of that city and bugger off to another city, allowing you to gain more influence and power.<br /> <br /> If the Hunter is a dumbass that attacks a vampire without intelligence, he will likely die, but he will have died of his stupidity, not because of your actions. The Hunter would have likely found evidence of the less humane vampire eventually, and you merely gave him the intelligence necessary to accomplish his goal (the hunting of vampires) without endangering yourself. After all, how else are you supposed to help Hunters find the less humane vampires without giving him a chance to kill you? It is not like he will trust you if you go up and tell him about the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:02:28-07:00","id":957790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=957782#post957782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But people have control over their actions and, even if you can reasonably predict their responses, they bear the entire weight of guilt for their actions as long as they are not under your control. A Hunter has a choice to invade the lair of a vampire when the only evidence is a trail of drained animal bodies. A Hunter has the choice to oppose the gang members or to surrender his money or weapons. A Hunter has the choice to attack the police when they arrest him or to trust in the judicial system (planted weapons will likely not lead to the death of the Hunter, though it may lead to his imprisonment).</div> </div> </div> </div> Realistically, I think here is the point where further dialogue between us on this topic is futile - you obviously feel that influencing someone to do something terrible means you bear no responsibility whatsoever for that subsequent terrible something, which is a position I flatly disagree with. Further, given the inherent subjectivity of personal morality it seems unlikely to me that either of us is particularly likely to sway the other.<br /> <br /> I mean, yes, people have control over their actions. But people choose their responses based on their circumstances - and you are a part of those circumstances. Therefore, you have control over the actions of others, which to me makes you responsible for the foreseeable consequences of your actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=957782#post957782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If a Hunter chooses to observe the lair of the less humane vampire and interferes when that vampire drags a helpless victim into their lair (or follows them on their hunting rounds and saves an innocent when the less humane vampire attacks them), then several good things may happen. First, the Hunter may save an innocent that you, as the humane vampire, could not save because you might harm the other vampire. Second, the Hunter may kill the inhumane vampire, potentially saving dozens or hundreds of innocent lives in the future, which you could not have done. Third, the Hunter may decide that he found the vampire of that city and bugger off to another city, allowing you to gain more influence and power.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Path of Humanity isn't about creating good outcomes. It may be objectively true that killing a serial killer makes the world a better, safer place - you're still rolling degeneration for lopping the bastard's head off and flushing his corpse down the drain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=957782#post957782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the Hunter is a dumbass that attacks a vampire without intelligence, he will likely die, but he will have died of his stupidity, not because of your actions.</div> </div> </div> </div> Regardless of your position on the morality of it, this doesn't logically follow. &quot;Not because of your actions&quot; - you told him where to find the vampire. If you hadn't, <i>he would not have died. </i>But for your actions, he would still be alive. Logically, you're responsible. Morally, you may not be, and that is manifestly where we disagree. But in terms of establishing causality, you're objectively mistaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11105,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","user":"Seviphas","date":".  Correcting layout errors. 08-25-2016, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:46:54-07:00","id":957853,"title":"","content":"In regards to torturing and killing in complicated way being &quot;pointless evil&quot; - the Nephandi could use such killings and tortures to increase their Spheres and in some cases even Arete; creating and charging magic items is another use. Some Nephandi might have suffering as foci for certain effects or rotes.<br /> Black Spiral Dancers could do it to create Fetishes, placate Spirits and learn or create new Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:42:52-07:00","id":957979,"title":"","content":"dont forget in the Red Talon tribe book, theirs the rites from the dieing cubs that uses torturing humans to wash away the lands taint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T19:54:58-07:00","id":958012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=957700#post957700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am guilty of the sins of people I do not control?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. What you aren't grasping is that there can be a multitude of guilty parties who bear responsibility for a single sin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Am I guilty of murder if I sell someone the guns they use to kill their wife? </div> </div> </div>If you do so knowing they will kill their wife with it, reasonably suspect they will, or actively -hope- they will (the closest to your example of 'lure the hunter to the lair of a feral vampire) then yes, you bear moral guilt and may also have some legal guilt as an accessory or conspirator depending on jurisidction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Am I guilty of murder if I sell someone the beer that sends them into alcohol poisoning? </div> </div> </div>Yes, if they die. If you willingly and freely sell an already dangerously intoxicated person the alcohol that tips them over the edge, you are in fact both morally (and in many jurisdictions, legally) responsible for their death. Arguably, as they lack the capacity to make decisions for themselves at such a degree of intoxication, you alone bear the responsibility for the decision - not them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Am I guilty of murder if I break up with someone and that causes them to commit suicide? </div> </div> </div>That depends on how you break up. If you are deliberately cruel, knowing they are in a fragile state, then yes - you bear some moral responsibility for what follows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When are the people who make the murderous or suicidal decisions guilty of their actions? </div> </div> </div>Morality is not a zero-sum game. Multiple parties can bear different degrees of moral responsibility for the same sin.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/854312-ideas-on-how-to-put-hunters-in-their-place-sadistic-evil-minds-wanted?p=957782#post957782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But people have control over their actions and, even if you can reasonably predict their responses, they bear the entire weight of guilt for their actions as long as they are not under your control.</div> </div> </div> </div>The argument is not that the person who does the action itself is not guilty. The argument is that you, as the orchestrator of that action, are also guilty.<br /> <br /> [quote[A Hunter has a choice to invade the lair of a vampire when the only evidence is a trail of drained animal bodies. A Hunter has the choice to oppose the gang members or to surrender his money or weapons.[/quote]<br /> <br /> None of these choices would take place if you did not deliberately engineer them. They are not random occurences beyond your control - they are circumstances you deliberately, knowingly, and with malice aforethought sought to create. It might surprise you but in most jurisdictions, the guilt attached isn't just moral - it's legal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Hunter has the choice to attack the police when they arrest him or to trust in the judicial system (planted weapons will likely not lead to the death of the Hunter, though it may lead to his imprisonment). </div> </div> </div>Except of course that you've framed them, itself a humanity sin, and then gone to the extent of planting a weapon used to kill a police officer in their possessions with the -explicit- intent that they will be killed or at least brutalized. No matter what choice the hunter makes, your action in bringing about the circumstances is sinful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a Hunter chooses to observe the lair of the less humane vampire and interferes when that vampire drags a helpless victim into their lair (or follows them on their hunting rounds and saves an innocent when the less humane vampire attacks them), then several good things may happen. First, the Hunter may save an innocent that you, as the humane vampire, could not save because you might harm the other vampire. Second, the Hunter may kill the inhumane vampire, potentially saving dozens or hundreds of innocent lives in the future, which you could not have done. Third, the Hunter may decide that he found the vampire of that city and bugger off to another city, allowing you to gain more influence and power. </div> </div> </div>None of which are compatible with your premise of 'let's lure them to a painful death.' Your explicit purpose is not to achieve good, your explicit purpose is for the hunter to die. Any incidental good that follows from your decision to arrange their death does not exculpate you of that original intention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Hunter is a dumbass that attacks a vampire without intelligence, he will likely die, but he will have died of his stupidity, not because of your actions. </div> </div> </div>Except in this situation, the only reason he's tracked that vampire is because you've deliberately left him an obvious trail. The only reason that vampire is on his radar and in his sights is because of your deliberate, intentional actions to bring about his death at its hands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Hunter would have likely found evidence of the less humane vampire eventually, and you merely gave him the intelligence necessary to accomplish his goal (the hunting of vampires) without endangering yourself. </div> </div> </div>No, you gave him a trail of misleading information to lead him to his death. Your purpose is not to get bad vampires killed - your purpose here is to use them to kill the hunter hassling you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After all, how else are you supposed to help Hunters find the less humane vampires without giving him a chance to kill you? It is not like he will trust you if you go up and tell him about the vampire. </div> </div> </div>I hear anonymous notes and email work pretty well for tipping people off, and can convey much more information than 'a trail of dead bodies'.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let me ask you a question. If you know someone's got a serious heroin addiction, are you morally responsible in your eyes for their death if you break into their house while they're at work and leave a bag of fentanyl-laced heroin on their coffee table with the express intention of them overdosing on it?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T21:23:45-07:00","id":958043,"title":"","content":"That is hardly equivalent. A better equivalency would be if you gave a drug addict money for food and they died from an overdose of heroin that they bought instead of food. Would you be guilty then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T21:55:07-07:00","id":958055,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't, as in your purported equivalency the death of the hunter is caused by them misusing your goodwill. The actual course of action we are discussing, which you advanced as a way to deal with pesky hunters, is to lure them to the nest of a feral vampire to be killed. There is no goodwill in that course of action, only deliberate and malicious intent to cause death or at least severe bodily harm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:44:47-07:00","id":958546,"title":"","content":"As a demon I rip their soul out and forge them into men's underwear. I remove the spirit's ability to defy me but still maintain it's personality and give it access to all the powers of the shorts. The shorts are able to manipulate gravity, open a portal to the shadow lands, and open a path to a location of my choice that will avoid the perceptions of anyone and have access to whatever powers the hunter had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":359,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","user":"Dezeroth","date":". 08-26-2016, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T04:43:18-07:00","id":959754,"title":"","content":"oh Another idea<br /> <br /> ways that a supernatural can both A: Accomplish some practical goal<br /> <br /> and B: Impress himself and the hunter with the size of his metaphorical penis.<br /> <br /> as its probaly best if B happens in the context of A... most supernaturals will probaly feel that way.<br /> <br /> Best idea I have is to tell him after hes sent out to act as CANNON Fodder, and is no longer of any use that he was USED.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T05:22:32-07:00","id":959762,"title":"","content":"It depends on who you are and what means do you have.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you are a Tzimisce you could just go to raw torture, shapeshifting them in living chairs or screaming tables, keeping them alive for years.<br /> Or maybe you could blood bound them, remove their spine and their legs's joint and make them crawl as they beg you for their daily drop of blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you are a Nosferatu or a Gangrel you could kidnap their beloved ones, closing them in a room full of rats and go for a creative use of animalism.<br /> <br /> As a Ventrue or a Lasombra you coul ruin their friends lives, getting them evicted by their houses, arrested with false charges or fired from their works.<br /> <br /> Best thing would be being a mage with Entropy 5: just shatter their faith, destroy everything they believe in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T09:42:05-07:00","id":959870,"title":"","content":"Tzimisce can be much more creative than that. They can kidnap the loved ones of hunters, use Vicissitude to give them great beauty (photographing the entire process) and sell them at a profit into white slavery overseas. They can then send the photos to the hunter and give the hunter the location where the hunter's loved ones can be found (and, if they wish to put salt in the wound, a free one way ticket to that location, in the hunter's name, that will leave within six hours of the hunter receiving the ticket). Few hunters are going to seek revenge until after they have rescued their loved ones from a lifetime of rape and, more likely than not, the criminal syndicates that own the loved ones of the hunter will kill the hunter off during the rescue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T18:17:29-07:00","id":963998,"title":"","content":"well ideas in particular, if your humanity is 3-5 your PROBALY above physical torture or murder, in most cases, but serving out a generous helping of Humble pie, is just fair right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T21:04:04-07:00","id":964051,"title":"","content":"Well, hm, putting Hunters in their place. Seems difficult.<br /> <br /> Per the Mandate of Heaven, the Chosen of the Unconquered Sun are supposed to rule all of Creation, so you'd need an extremely low-gen Healer Salubri, a Mage who's a Master of Spirit and Prime at least, or some equally potent spirit-manipulator to properly reawaken and empower their spark of divinity into a <i>proper</i> Exaltation. Charms could likely be emulated via Sphere Magick used to shape 'artifacts' out of the Hunter's soul as a temporary stopgap until they can reinvent their own Charms.<br /> <br /> A difficult and challenging problem indeed, even moreso than getting a Mage to Avatar 10 or the like. Though it should be possible; certain WoD splats are more potent in some respects than the Exalted Ones were and thus <i>theoretically</i> can reforge one of them. You'll need like, 10 or higher powerstat for whichever splat is used, though, this isn't child's play.<br /> <br /> I'll need to think about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T07:17:18-07:00","id":964268,"title":"","content":"Hunters are not Solar Exalted and the Earth is not Creation, no matter what the fluff says, because the metaphysics are radically different. Anyway, all you need to get rid of a Hunter is a ten person infantry squad. They have enough firepower to chew up even an advanced Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T12:36:56-07:00","id":964470,"title":"","content":"Well, yes, that's why you need to exert actual effort rather than just looking at it and going &quot;welp it's done&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:53:36-07:00","id":964674,"title":"","content":"As a vampire, like myself,you may use the advantage of age to pull some of the old classics out of the bag (it worked then, it works now), here's one that's morbid in it's simplcity and should be child's play for those of you with a gift for beasts. Dip the chosen victim in honey and drop them into a tub of milk, bound of course, preferably with metal, you will see why in a moment. Then just leave for a while. If you are aware of these new gadgets called 'video cameras' and have know new books or intrigues of the court, to deal with you may monitor the process as the insects and rats descend upon your hunter fellow. The rats will nibble at bits and extremities as the insects will burrow into their body. Soon all your victim will feel is a slow and complete pain as well as the feeling of the bugs engorging themselves on blood and honey, growing from within the hunter's own flesh. Some say the victim can feel the insects crawling around in their brain after a while, isn't that a thought! Now if you are unfortunate, after a few days of this the victim may pass away from dehydration or hunger, but it's possible to keep him alive, slowly dying over quite a bit of time. Now this is but one of many of the old methods (although it is MY favorite), but then again who does not love a good old bronze bull over the hearth! Now if those get stale that new contraption of the kine, 'the internet' has a handy collection noted by one Wiki Pedia, quite an active scholar that one, if a bit of an odd name. Anyway with this and it's like I'm sure you'll have no shortage of appropriate punishments. Show them to scuff up your floors again, eh!<br /> <br /> -From the journals of Nicostrato Cisternino, Lasombra Cardinal of Sicily, aged 971","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 09-06-2016, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}